+**What the positive control shows, and what it does not.** The registered contrast and label rule returned DETECTED in a case where the answer was known in advance: retrieval must carry image information to an image-blind generator. This is evidence that the arms, the scoring path for these rows and the bootstrap and label rules can detect a retrieval-specific effect when one is present. The effect is about 8.5 times the SESOI of +2.0, so the control says nothing about sensitivity near +2.0: the planned chance of DETECTED at a true +2.0 on OV-dev-B stays about 0.49 at the planned standard error of Qwen2.5-VL-7B (registration §7.13; values are for m = 1). It has no negative control, so it says nothing about how often DETECTED is returned when no effect is present; the `rand` d1 − d2 placebo rows of Section 6.10.5 are the study's only such check, and one of them, Aya-Vision-8B's on OV-dev-B, was flagged. It does not re-validate or strengthen the rows of Section 6.10.3, neither the two nominated τ_pair claims nor the τ_marg rows: those rest on their own registration, scoring path and labels, while LMCap ran on another model, pipeline and scoring path, on another machine. It says nothing about the `perm` arm's validity for those rows or about how their τ_sel splits, nothing about LMCap's published numbers or the authors' system, and nothing about any test set or about XM-dev500.
+
+**LMCap's split on OV-dev-B.** LMCap's τ_pair was +17.40 [15.48, 19.41] (p̃ = 1/2,001, its floor, m = 1): DETECTED; first look; computed after τ_sel, in the registered order; not the split of a τ_sel known when the rule was registered. LMCap's τ_marg was −0.48 [−1.27, 0.28] (90% interval [−1.14, 0.17]): NEGLIGIBLE, smaller than 2.0 points in either direction (the 90% interval lies inside ±2.0); NEGLIGIBLE does not mean zero. First look; computed after τ_sel, in the registered order; not the split of a τ_sel known when the rule was registered. The registration's planning values for this label belong to Qwen2.5-VL-7B (standard error about 1.03 on OV-dev-B, where NEGLIGIBLE needs a point within about ±0.3 of zero; registration §7.13; values are for m = 1); no planning value was registered for LMCap. LMCap's retrieval-specific effect on OV-dev-B lies in the pairing of captions to the query (τ_pair DETECTED), while the part given by the set of captions shown is smaller than 2.0 points in either direction (τ_marg NEGLIGIBLE): the same label pattern as the τ_pair and τ_marg rows of Qwen2.5-VL-7B and InternVL3-8B on this set (Section 6.10.3). This is a description, not a check of those rows.
+
+**The image format on OV-dev-B.** Qwen2.5-VL-7B's image-format τ_sel was +6.36 [4.30, 8.46] (p̃ = 1/2,001, its floor, m = 1): DETECTED; first look; its `ret_img` side had been seen in the exploration runs of the Flickr30K registration. Beside it, the text-example τ_sel of the same backbone on this set was +8.27 [6.54, 10.11], DETECTED, with its own labels (Table 16). The two rows were decoded on different machines, in different blocks. No difference or ratio between them is computed, and neither is called larger: that would be an unregistered contrast between prompt formats.
+
+**XM-dev500.** Every XM-dev500 row of Table 18 has no registered rule (registration §7.8): its label is printed and no conclusion is drawn, for the DETECTED rows as well. Qwen2.5-VL-7B's image-format row there is UNRESOLVED: the data neither establish an effect of at least +2.0 nor bound it inside ±2.0. Beside it, the text-example row of Table S21 is printed with its own label; no difference is computed.
